meta {
  name: saveSupplier
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: https://{{customer}}.{{domain}}/jsonrpc
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "method": "saveSupplier",
    "params": {
      "supplier_name": "Main Supplier",
      "external_supplier_id": "MAIN",
      "country_code": "NL"
    },
    "id": 1
  }
}

docs {
  Create or update a supplier

  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `supplier_id` | integer (nullable) | no | Internal ID of the supplier; omit to create a new supplier |
  | `external_supplier_id` | string (nullable) | no | Unique short code identifying the supplier (your system's reference) |
  | `supplier_name` | string (nullable) | no | Display name of the supplier |
  | `company_name` | string (nullable) | no | Registered company name |
  | `company_name_2` | string (nullable) | no | Second line of the company name |
  | `address` | string (nullable) | no | Street address |
  | `city` | string (nullable) | no | City |
  | `postal_code` | string (nullable) | no | Postal or ZIP code |
  | `country_code` | string (nullable) | no | ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code |
  | `gln` | string (nullable) | no | Global Location Number (GS1 GLN, 13 digits) |

  **Example: Create a supplier**. Omit supplier_id to create; provide it to update.

  ```json
  {
    "jsonrpc": "2.0",
    "method": "saveSupplier",
    "params": {
      "supplier_name": "Main Supplier",
      "external_supplier_id": "MAIN",
      "country_code": "NL"
    },
    "id": 1
  }
  ```

  Result:

  ```json
  {
    "supplier_id": 5
  }
  ```
}
